    56	## 4. Nulls and rules (per judge and reading, fixed before any planted unit is scored)
    57	
    58	- The 89 honest units scored; **11.12(d)** (`stage3_views.defect_check`: refused or errored above 0.05; one score over half; fewer than five distinct scores above the median; a truncated packet or a failed applier check). **A defective null stops that (judge, reading) without rewrite (reading):** its planted units are not scored; the other reading of the same judge continues when its own null is clean (each reading is its own instrument with its own null).
    59	- **Author rule** at **B = 0.10** (`judge_opus_q1q2.author_rule`: the author's maximum over their honest dossier pairs, account-day weights over all 50 accounts, `stage3_thresholds.author_level_threshold`, tie seed 20261112, the threshold bootstrap beside); the unit rule at 0.10 beside, not used for flags. Written to `b1/b1-null.json` with the null's rows and committed by hash before the first planted unit of that judge is scored.
    60	- **A planted author is flagged** when the maximum of the planted dossier unit's score and the author's honest dossier pairs on the **other** class documents (the same judge and reading) reaches the author rule, the tie drawn by the author's name (the sealed P_author reading). A plant is flagged when any planted author is.
    61	
    62	## 5. Estimate, caps, re-base
    63	
    64	- **Estimate before any call** (`--dry-run`, `b1/b1-estimate.json`): every packet rendered; Sonnet by the sealed convention (`stage3_views.estimate`: 2.15 characters per token, 230 output tokens); Opus 4.8 with input at 2.15 characters per token and output at its **realised mean output tokens on the re-plant's O_diff cache** (534; the closest whole-document unit it has scored), with its re-plant P_author mean and the O_diff maximum beside.
    65	- **Stop line $50, hard cap $60** (Aravind's decision above). No call if the combined estimate exceeds $50. **First-batch re-base:** each judge's first 20 isolated null units are scored first; the realised mean cost per unit re-scales every (reading, unit set) of that judge; the run continues only if the projection (every dollar paid under `b1/` + this judge's re-based remainder + the plain estimate of a judge not started) is at or under $50; the note is written to the estimate file with a timestamp, never overwritten. A judge's allowance is 1.5 × the larger of its estimate and its re-based total; a client's spend cap is the smaller of the judge's remaining allowance and $60 minus every dollar paid.
    66	- **Order** (each step its own invocation): Sonnet null (iso: first batch, then the rest; live), Opus 4.8 null (the same), `b1-null.json` committed; then re-plant (Sonnet iso, live; Opus 4.8 iso, live), v2, v3. Errored units are re-asked once by a rerun before the results are written. Bedrock credentials checked before the run; no key printed.
